%% Topic 6 answers — examiner's-eye box; included by T6QA and the compiled QA volume.

::: eye | Topic 6 is a topic of judgements
Almost every question here asks you to **judge**: pros and cons (2016), "comment" (2017), "do you think" (2018), "useful or preferential" (2020), "is it showing results?" (2021), "in your opinion" (2022), "is it a human right?" (2024). Notice how the same core material is re-cut each time — **Pitkin** (descriptive vs substantive representation), **Dahlerup** (fast track, critical mass), the **quota history** (1956, 1962, 1973, 1985, the lapse, 2002, 2017), the **caucus laws** of 2010–2016, and the **2024** numbers (60 reserved seats, 306 women candidates, 11 winners, 9.94 million fewer women voters). Every answer ends with a clear **view** and **reforms**: direct election, a stronger candidate quota in winnable seats, and party democracy.
:::
